cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Latent Geometry vs. Prediction Error: a pre-registered, leakage-free
  detection-latency benchmark for video world models
message: If you use this harness or benchmark, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Faisal Parvez"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered evaluation harness testing whether the internal
  representation geometry of a frozen video world model crosses an alarm
  threshold sooner than the model's own prediction error. Provides a synthetic
  anomaly benchmark, three online geometry probes, two prediction-error
  baselines (including the model's own pretraining objective evaluated
  causally), survival analysis of detection latency, and a model-agnostic
  adapter contract enforced by a parameterised test suite. On the registered
  experiment the verdict is negative: two geometry probes beat the model's own
  loss significantly but lose to a ridge predictor reading the same latent
  sequence.
keywords:
  - world models
  - anomaly detection
  - detection latency
  - V-JEPA
  - survival analysis
  - pre-registration
  - representation geometry
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/faisalhacks/latent-surprise-race"
